  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 15 actions (src/actions.js) and 5 boolean feedbacks (src/feedbacks.js). Both files register their definitions in a single call, no definitions are generated at runtime.",
    "The module talks OSC to the console (TCP 3032, or TCP SLIP 3037 with the \"Use TCP SLIP\" setting; src/constants.js, companion/HELP.md). Variables (encoder wheels, labels, cue state) are not catalogued; they are built from src/param_map.js and src/variables.js.",
    "Nearly all fields are text inputs with useVariables; numeric values are therefore strings. The regular expressions are the values of Regex.FLOAT_OR_INT (/^([0-9]+)(\\.[0-9]+)?$/) and Regex.NUMBER (/^\\d+$/) from @companion-module/base 1.15.0 (dist/module-api/enums.js), plus the inline pattern for intensity values.",
    "The feedback macroisfired declares regex: Regex.INT (src/feedbacks.js:19). Regex.INT is not defined in @companion-module/base 1.15.0, so the field has no effective pattern and the catalog records none.",
    "Feedback comparisons are strict string equality against the state reported by the console (for example feedback.options.list === instanceState.cue_active_list). A cue number such as \"1\" and \"1.0\" therefore do not match.",
    "press_key sends OSC /eos/key/<key> (key names: see the module help); custom_osc and send_multiple send arbitrary OSC paths and can trigger anything the console accepts.",
    "sub_bump and softkey: \"Press and Release\" sends no argument, \"Press and Hold\" sends 1.0 and \"Release\" sends 0.0 (src/actions.js:324-334, 382-392).",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~1.15.0: options do not support expressions."
  ],
